Rust dependencies
-----------------

The tool is built from crates published to crates.io. Each carries its own
licence in its published manifest. Where a crate ships an Apache-2.0 notice,
section 4 of that licence requires the notice to travel with a binary built
from it. Those notices are in the crates themselves, and a binary distributor
should collect them from the dependency tree rather than from this file. No
automated licence check runs over the dependency graph.

Documentation site
------------------

The pages under `docs/` are built with VitePress and Vue. Those packages and
their dependencies carry their own licences in `docs/bun.lock`, and a built
site should carry the notices those licences require.
